==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{OCS.|ru}} {{term|зима|lang=cu}} ("winter") < {{PIE.|ru}} '''*gheim-''' ("snow", "winter"). Cognate with Sanskrit '''heman''' ("in winter"}, Hittite '''gimmanza''', Greek {{IPAchar|[[χεῖμα]]}}, and Lithuanian [[ziema]] (all meaning "winter"). Possibly related to Persian [[زمستان|زِمِستان]] (zemestān).

===Noun===
'''зима''' (zimá) {{f}}

#[[winter]]

